                <pb facs="1077" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg983"/>

                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">B.—Reciprocity with foreign nations
                        for the payment of tonnage and port dues.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">a.</hi> Royal decree of June 4, 1868, establishing
                    reciprocity of dues for the payment of tonnage or navigation and port dues in
                    the islands of Cuba, Porto Rico, and the Philippines, with respect to the
                    vessels of all nations which in their respective territories <pb facs="1078"
                        n="984" xml:id="pg984"/> or colonial possessions grant the same benefit to
                    vessels of the Spanish merchant service. * * *</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi>. 1. The vessels of all nations which
                    grant a similar benefit within their respective territories and colonial
                    possessions to Spanish merchant vessels proceeding from the ports of Spain and
                    adjacent islands shall be equalized in the islands of Cuba, Porto Rico, and the
                    Philippines with Spanish vessels in regard to the exaction of tonnage and port
                    dues.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
